    "intro_html":  "Loubia is the green bean stew that shows up on tables from Beirut to Amman, tomato and allspice and cinnamon simmered down until the beans go soft and the sauce goes deep. Turkey breast stands in for the usual stew beef, and it soaks up the spice just as well for a fraction of the money. Over rice it lands at \u003cstrong\u003e569 calories and 44 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.41\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost), and it reheats better on day four than it did on day one.",
